  "changelog": "Drafting fixes\n  - Fixed the \"Hi ,\" greeting bug \u2014 when sender-name extraction returned an empty\n    first name, the greeting rendered with a dangling space before the comma.\n    Now collapses cleanly to \"Hi,\" instead. Regression test pins this.\n\n  Ops / operability\n  - New `/readyz` endpoint for launchd/health probes (reports DB resolvability).\n  - `/healthz` now returns the runtime version. A regression test pins that\n    `/healthz`, `/readyz`, and `/api/config` all report the same `get_version()`,\n    so the version drift across runtime surfaces that used to bite occasionally\n    can't quietly come back.\n  - `youos doctor` now distinguishes \"Python `mlx_lm` package not importable in\n    this venv\" from \"global `mlx_lm` binary on PATH\" \u2014 the error no longer\n    reads as contradicting a visible `which mlx_lm`.\n\n  Skill metadata + safety surfacing\n  - SKILL.md gains a prominent **Safety & impact** section near the top\n    (sensitive Gmail/Docs/WhatsApp ingestion, install runs local code, opt-in\n    launchd, opt-in nightly, optional cloud fallback + strict-local instructions),\n    plus a **Naming** line clarifying that *<First>OS* is your local instance\n    under `YOUOS_DATA_DIR`, not a fork of the project.\n  - `clawhub.json` no longer references screenshot/demo assets that aren't\n    inside the strict text-only bundle (the homepage repo resolves them).\n\n  Requires Apple Silicon + Python 3.11+. Public beta.",
